# Printers on folk-sva.
#
# The Canon PIXMA lives on SVA's DHCP and its address moves; the cron
# job ~/bin/repair-printer.sh re-points the CUPS queue at it every 10
# minutes (SVA's WLAN blocks mDNS, so it has to be found by scanning).
#
# When the Canon is off the network entirely, print/print.folk falls
# back to the thermal strip printer instead of queueing a sheet that
# will never come out. See print/strip.folk.

Claim printer Pixma is the default printer
Claim paper format letter is the default paper format

# Deliberately NOT "is a receipt printer": that predicate routes to
# esc-pos.folk, which expects a networked printer on port 9100. This
# one is USB, driven through CUPS as a raw queue.
Claim printer ThermalPrinter is a thermal strip printer
